WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:18.707
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June fifth, which is Environment Day in Japan. It's a day to stop and think about the planet and how we treat it. In fact, all of June is treated as a month for the environment here. Let's listen.

00:00:19.307 --> 00:00:22.068
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:00:22.768 --> 00:00:27.568
<v News>6月5日は、「環境の日」です。

00:00:28.268 --> 00:00:34.268
<v News>環境の日は、地球の自然について考える日です。

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:41.256
<v News>日本では、6月を「環境月間」と呼んでいます。

00:00:41.956 --> 00:00:48.652
<v News>この1か月、日本のいろいろな所で、イベントがあります。

00:00:49.351 --> 00:00:54.512
<v News>たとえば、町のごみを拾う活動があります。

00:00:55.212 --> 00:00:58.643
<v News>木を植えるイベントもあります。

00:00:59.344 --> 00:01:05.055
<v News>川や海をきれいにする活動も、人気があります。

00:01:05.756 --> 00:01:11.900
<v News>学校でも、子どもたちが環境について勉強します。

00:01:12.599 --> 00:01:17.808
<v News>今、世界では、暑い日が増えています。

00:01:18.507 --> 00:01:23.188
<v News>プラスチックのごみも、大きな問題です。

00:01:23.888 --> 00:01:28.975
<v News>レジ袋を使わない人も、増えてきました。

00:01:29.676 --> 00:01:35.147
<v News>一人一人ができることは、小さいかもしれません。

00:01:35.847 --> 00:01:42.640
<v News>でも、ごみを減らしたり、電気を大切に使ったりできます。

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:48.500
<v News>買い物には、自分のかばんを持っていきましょう。

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:56.135
<v News>政府は、「みんなで環境のことを考えましょう」と話しています。

00:01:56.835 --> 00:01:58.468
<v Host>Let's break it down.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:04.540
<v Slow>6月5日は、「環境の日」です。

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.691
<v Host>June fifth is Environment Day.

00:02:08.292 --> 00:02:10.668
<v Vocab>環境

00:02:11.068 --> 00:02:17.139
<v Host>It means environment — the natural world around us, the air, water, and land.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:24.604
<v Slow>環境の日は、地球の自然について考える日です。

00:02:25.403 --> 00:02:29.123
<v Host>Environment Day is a day to think about the Earth's nature.

00:02:29.723 --> 00:02:31.860
<v Vocab>自然

00:02:32.259 --> 00:02:38.475
<v Host>It means nature. Think mountains, rivers, forests — the world not made by people.

00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:44.979
<v Slow>たとえば、町のごみを拾う活動があります。

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:50.075
<v Host>For example, there are activities to pick up trash around town.

00:02:50.675 --> 00:02:52.620
<v Vocab>ごみ

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:59.379
<v Host>It means trash or garbage. A very everyday word you'll see on bins all over Japan.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.891
<v Slow>木を植えるイベントもあります。

00:03:04.692 --> 00:03:07.379
<v Host>There are also events for planting trees.

00:03:07.979 --> 00:03:10.139
<v Vocab>植える

00:03:10.539 --> 00:03:15.243
<v Host>It means to plant — putting a tree or seed into the ground so it can grow.

00:03:15.843 --> 00:03:21.795
<v Slow>今、世界では、暑い日が増えています。

00:03:22.596 --> 00:03:26.243
<v Host>Right now, hot days are increasing around the world.

00:03:26.843 --> 00:03:29.075
<v Vocab>世界

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:34.852
<v Host>It means world. Add it to a topic and you've zoomed out to the whole planet.

00:03:35.451 --> 00:03:40.780
<v Slow>プラスチックのごみも、大きな問題です。

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.747
<v Host>Plastic trash is also a big problem.

00:03:45.348 --> 00:03:47.604
<v Vocab>問題

00:03:48.003 --> 00:03:52.756
<v Host>It means problem or issue. It's also the word for a question on a test.

00:03:53.355 --> 00:04:01.108
<v Slow>でも、ごみを減らしたり、電気を大切に使ったりできます。

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:06.252
<v Host>But we can do things like reduce trash and use electricity carefully.

00:04:06.852 --> 00:04:09.156
<v Vocab>減らす

00:04:09.556 --> 00:04:14.355
<v Host>It means to reduce or cut down. The opposite is to increase.

00:04:14.955 --> 00:04:22.875
<v Slow>政府は、「みんなで環境のことを考えましょう」と話しています。

00:04:23.675 --> 00:04:27.851
<v Host>The government is saying, let's all think about the environment together.

00:04:28.451 --> 00:04:30.875
<v Vocab>考える

00:04:31.276 --> 00:04:36.795
<v Host>It means to think or to consider. Here, to think things over carefully as a group.

00:04:37.396 --> 00:04:40.396
<v Host>Let's listen to the full story one more time.

